r listening-sockets) as a dependency of aide-common's mail-reporting feature; this is an expected side effect of enabling AIDE's mail-based check reporting, not an unrelated exposure. No failed or conflicting services were observed in either snapshot, and package health remained consistent (manager=dpkg, no reported inconsistency).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c2f1ca6b9f5f447c\",\"cmd-3292f6e53bcc439a\",\"cmd-fc749fe3356343c0\",\"cmd-7937ac1731bb4fe5\",\"cmd-a8474a8bb2bd4b4e\",\"cmd-fec89c330a4b4a86\",\"cmd-5eb96af8cb3948cf\",\"cmd-d10094bf26a3457c\",\"cmd-4fa82bdd7b9f46cf\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor established a working AIDE integrity baseline for /etc on node1, verified the default configuration recursively covers /etc, and directly proved detection/reporting behavior by injecting and then removing a test file and observing the corresponding 'Added entries' report and subsequent clean state. A daily systemd timer is enabled for ongoing scheduled reporting. Independently, the mandatory provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol was executed cleanly: pre-restart healthy baseline (boot_id, aide.db checksum, active timer) was captured, `shutdown -r now` was acknowledged, the node became briefly unreachable, and post-restart state showed a changed boot_id, an unchanged aide.db checksum, an active/enabled timer, and a fresh scoped check reporting no differences across the same 87,362 entries — fully demonstrating recovery. Minor operational inefficiencies (a stalled background check requiring repeated kill attempts, iterative temp config files) were all fully cleaned up and did not affect the final state.\",\"limitations\":[\"Only a single restart cycle was captured for node1 (the sole managed node); no additional nodes exist in this topology to cross-check the restart protocol.\",\"The task instruction did not expli